INSTALL — Anteater Poker
Team 23 | EECS 22L | University of California, Irvine


DEPENDENCIES
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  - GCC (C11 or later)
  - GTK+3 development libraries
  - POSIX threads (pthreads) — included with glibc on Linux
  - GNU Make
  - pkg-config

On the EECS Linux servers (bondi, crystalcove, etc.) these are
already available. On a fresh Ubuntu/Debian machine:

  sudo apt-get install gcc make libgtk-3-dev pkg-config


PACKAGE LAYOUT
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  poker/
    Makefile        top-level build/package targets
    README          overview and quick start
    COPYRIGHT       license / copyright
    INSTALL         this file
    src/            source code and src/Makefile
    bin/            compiled executables (after `make`)
    doc/            PDF documentation


BUILDING FROM SOURCE  (Source release: Poker_Beta_src.tar.gz)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  1. Unpack the source archive:
       gtar xvzf Poker_Beta_src.tar.gz

  2. Enter the project directory:
       cd poker

  3. Build all executables:
       make

     Executables are placed in poker/bin/:
       poker/bin/poker_server
       poker/bin/poker_client

  4. Run the unit tests:
       make test

  5. Clean build artifacts:
       make clean


RUNNING  (Binary release: Poker_Beta.tar.gz)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  1. Unpack the binary archive:
       gtar xvzf Poker_Beta.tar.gz

  2. Enter the project directory:
       cd poker

  3. Read the user manual (optional):
       evince doc/Poker_UserManual.pdf

  4. Start the server (runs in the background):
       ./bin/poker_server &

  5. Launch the client (one per player):
       ./bin/poker_client

  NOTE: If the binary release was built on a different platform,
  rebuild from source on this machine first with `make`
  (the binaries are then regenerated in bin/).


CUSTOM PORT
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  ./bin/poker_server 9001 &
  (clients enter port 9001 on the login screen)


NETWORK PLAY
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  - Run poker_server on one machine.
  - Each player runs poker_client on their own machine.
  - Enter the server machine's IP address on the login screen.
  - Ensure the chosen port (default 9000) is not blocked by a firewall.


UNINSTALLING
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  pkill poker_server
  pkill poker_client
  cd ..
  rm -rf poker/

INSTALLING ON MAC LAPTOPS/DESKTOPS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
	STEP 1: Check is Homebrew is installed on your Mac using the following command: 
		brew --version
	
	STEP 2: If that says command not found you'll need to install Homebrew using the following command:
		/bin/bash -c "$(curl -fsSL https://row.githubusercontent.com/Homebrew/install/HEAD/install.sh)"

	STEP 3: Then install GTK, pkg-config, and XQuartz using the below commands:
		1) "brew install gtk+3 pkg-config"
		2) "brew install --cask xquartz
	
	STEP 4: It is important to reboot your Mac after the installation is complete (step 3) otherwise XQuartz won't work
	
	STEP 5: Extract the (.tar.gz) file and place the folder in your desktop
	 
	STEP 6: Open VsCode and go to (File) on the top of your Mac screen, then (Open Folder), then choose the poker folder from Desktop
	
	STEP 7: In the VsCode terminal run the following command: "Make"

	STEP 8: If it succeeds, you will have two programs in (poker/bin/) which are (poker_server) and (poker_client) 

	STEP 9: In your VsCode terminal, you should run the server using the following command: "./bin/poker_server &"

	STEP 10: Also in your VsCode terminal, you should run the client using the following command: "./bin/poker_client"

	STEP 11: Log in and have fun!
			
